#X text 20 900 MIC PROBE -- can an SM58 go straight into the Organelle's input? Knob 1 Pd's gain 0 to +40 dB. Knob 2 the gate: off at the bottom \, then -75 to -20 dBFS. Knob 3 the chip's input gain \, Capture 0 to 15 at 1.5 dB a step with the -6 dB attenuator off. The lowest C records 10 s of the raw input to /tmp/mic.wav. The knobs' positions at load are ignored: it starts at 0 dB \, gate off \, Capture 15. Not part of Cut It: loading Cut It puts the input gain back., f 120;
#X text 20 980 The mic goes to both outputs. Feedback: start with the mixer channel and knob 1 low., f 120;
